 loc="to verify: Daskalakis et al., open problems on the measurement count.",
 url="https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.04237",
 why="Generative priors replaced sparsity in many inverse problems; random-weight generators are the solvable model of why gradient descent recovers signals.",
 st="Partly solved (constant expansion); optimal measurement count open as far as the writer knows.",
